\begin{exercise}[$\star\star$]\label{ex:shuffle}
A deck of $52$ cards is cut into two halves of $26$, which are interleaved perfectly. In an \emph{out-shuffle} the top card stays on top; in an \emph{in-shuffle} it becomes second. Number the positions $0$ (top) to $51$. Show that the out-shuffle sends the card in position $i$ to position $2i\bmod 51$ for $i\le50$, and fixes position $51$; then show that $8$ out-shuffles restore the deck. How many in-shuffles are needed? (Use Volume~2.)
\end{exercise}

